          "title": "Sliding Window and Frequency Counts",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Window",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Keep a range ==[l, r]== and update state incrementally",
                "{green:O(n)} instead of O(n^2) re-scanning"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Fixed size k",
                "Variable"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Grow",
                  "add `s[r]`",
                  "expand `r`"
                ],
                [
                  "Shrink",
                  "drop `s[r-k]` once longer than k",
                  "move `l` while invalid"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Longest Without Repeats",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Map `last[c]` holds the last index of each char",
                "Jump ==l = max(l, last[c]+1)==",
                "{blue:O(n)} time, O(alphabet) space"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "last = {}; l = best = 0",
                "for r, c in enumerate(s):",
                "    l = max(l, last.get(c, -1) + 1)",
                "    last[c] = r",
                "    best = max(best, r - l + 1)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Anagram Windows",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Compare a 26-slot count array (or map) of window vs pattern",
                "Track a ==matched== counter; a slide touches only two slots",
                "Each slide is {purple:O(1)}, not an array re-compare"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Moving `l` backwards on a jump: use ==max==",
                "Not deleting a zero count from a map before comparing",
                "Updating the answer before the window is valid"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Palindromes and Expand Around Centre",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Palindromes and Expand Around Centre",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Centres",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Palindrome = reads the ==same both ways==",
                "Length n gives ==2n-1 centres==",
                "{green:n} single chars (odd length)",
                "{blue:n-1} gaps between chars (even length)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Expand and Count",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Set `l`, `r`; while `l>=0`, `r<n`, `s[l]==s[r]`: `l--`, `r++`",
                "==O(n^2)== time, ==O(1)== space",
                "Longest: try `(i,i)` and `(i,i+1)`, keep best",
                "Length after loop = ==r-l-1==",
                "Count: +1 per successful step, all 2n-1 centres"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def expand(s,l,r):",
                " while l>=0 and r<len(s) and s[l]==s[r]: l,r=l-1,r+1",
                " return r-l-1",
                "def longest(s):",
                " best=(0,0)",
                " for i in range(len(s)):",
                "  n=max(expand(s,i,i),expand(s,i,i+1))",
                "  if n>best[1]: best=(i-(n-1)//2,n)"
              ],
              "note": "best = (start, length)"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Alternatives and Bugs",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Time",
                "Space"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Expand",
                  "O(n^2)",
                  "O(1)"
                ],
                [
                  "DP table",
                  "O(n^2)",
                  "O(n^2)"
                ],
                [
                  "Manacher",
                  "O(n)",
                  "O(n), harder"
                ],
                [
                  "Two pointers",
                  "O(n)",
                  "O(1), one string"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common bug",
              "text": "Forgetting the ==even-length centre== `(i,i+1)` misses `abba`."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why 2n-1 centres?** n chars plus n-1 gaps",
                "**Space of expansion?** O(1), no table",
                "**Faster than O(n^2)?** Manacher, O(n)"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
