    {
      "title": "Rabin-Karp Rolling Hash",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rabin-Karp Rolling Hash",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Hash and Roll",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Hash every length-`m` window, compare with the ==pattern hash==",
                "On a hash match, **verify** the real substrings",
                "Expected ==O(n+m)==, worst case **O(n*m)**",
                "`h = s[0]*B^(m-1) + ... + s[m-1]` taken mod a large prime `M`",
                "Precompute `B^(m-1) mod M` once for the roll",
                "Roll in O(1): `h = ((h - s[i]*B^(m-1)) * B + s[i+m]) mod M`",
                "Add `M` before the final mod so `h` never goes negative"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def rk(t,p,B=256,M=1000003):",
                "    m=len(p); hi=pow(B,m-1,M); hp=h=0",
                "    for i in range(m): hp=(hp*B+ord(p[i]))%M; h=(h*B+ord(t[i]))%M",
                "    for i in range(len(t)-m+1):",
                "        if h==hp and t[i:i+m]==p: print(i)",
                "        if i+m<len(t): h=((h-ord(t[i])*hi)*B+ord(t[i+m]))%M",
                "rk('abracadabra','abra')"
              ],
              "note": "hash hit, then compare substrings"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "0",
                "7"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Collisions and Fit",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Equal hashes can be a ==false positive==, so always compare the text",
                "Make collisions rare: **large prime** `M` or a ==double hash=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Rabin-Karp",
                "KMP"
              ],
              "rows": [
